      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Well-child visit — Behind schedule:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if a child comes under care for the first time at any point, or items weren't done at the suggested age, bring the schedule up to date as soon as possible."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Well-child visit — Exam:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " an age-appropriate physical exam at each visit, with the infant totally unclothed and older children undressed and suitably draped."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Well-child visit — Adolescents:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " screen for depression and suicide risk, making every effort to preserve the adolescent's confidentiality."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Well-child visit — Substance use:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a recommended tool to assess alcohol, tobacco and nicotine, marijuana and other substance use (including opioids) is CRAFFT (crafft.org)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Prenatal and newborn visits — Prenatal visit:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " recommended for high-risk parents, first-time parents and those who ask; include anticipatory guidance, pertinent medical history, and the benefits of breastfeeding and planned feeding method."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Prenatal and newborn visits — Newborn follow-up:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " evaluate newborns within 3 to 5 days of birth and within 48 to 72 hours after hospital discharge, including feeding and jaundice."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Prenatal and newborn visits — Newborn history:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " the HPI can include the mother's pregnancy and the infant's status at birth; social history focuses on family structure, and family history on congenital anomalies and hereditary disorders."
     }
    ]
   }
